    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d357">

                <pb facs="0634" n="500" xml:id="pg500"/>

                <head>No. 357.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. McLane.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-01-13"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 13,
                        1888</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 287.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: By a dispatch dated November 10, 1887, from
                    Mr. Pratt, United States consul at Zanzibar, I have been informed that a new
                    treaty was under negotiation between the French Government and the King of
                    Johanna, one of the Comoro islands, situated in the northern entrance to the
                    Mozambique Channel. And a statement has subsequently appeared in the public
                    prints that France has taken possession of that island.</p>
                <p>I have, therefore, to instruct you with a view to the protection of the rights of
                    certain American citizens there resident, to obtain, if possible, from the
                    French foreign office an exact statement of the relations now subsisting between
                    the two governments, and copies of any treaties France may have concluded with
                    the King of Johanna.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F. Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
